        {
          "id": "2123963723627077959",
          "text": "If our absurdly oversized Council Districts served to magically dilute NIMBY voices why are we governed by a bunch of NIMBYs?",
          "url": "https://x.com/UnrigLA/status/2123963723627077959",
          "lang": "en",
          "createdAt": "2026-11-21T02:16:27.000Z",
          "conversationId": "2123963723627077959",
          "inReplyToId": null,
          "author": {
            "id": "1022564507971801088",
            "username": "UnrigLA",
            "name": "Unrig LA",
            "verified": false,
            "followersCount": 16613,
            "profileImageUrl": "https://pbs.twimg.com/profile_images/1179148691996721152/z38zFDv5_normal.jpg"
          },
          "likeCount": 20,
          "retweetCount": 1,
          "replyCount": 3,
          "viewCount": 1118,
          "quoteCount": 1,
          "bookmarkCount": 1,
          "media": [],
          "entities": {
            "hashtags": [],
            "mentions": [],
            "urls": []
          },
          "article": null,
          "quotedPost": {
            "id": "2123910888071799131",
            "text": "🥱 Same story every few years.  I was literally on Colorado blvd last night going to Yogurtland on Eagle Rock blvd.   DSA Councilwoman Jurado sounds very normal in her comments in this LAT story, which is good.  Eagle Rock votes, the homes above Colorado Blvd are all worth millions, tend to be more conservative in their voting patterns (still Dem tho).  Ysabel did well in those precincts since they tend to always vote against City Hall incumbents, and now she’s reflecting their perspective.  \n\nThe one funny item about city council expansion is, established HOA’s wholly within a district get stronger, because their impact is greater now in a small geographic area, your seeing the strength of Eagle Rock homeowners in terms of a bus lane, think forward now to Eagle Rock being in a smaller district.  That voice gains weight.   Will be interesting to observe and see.",
            "url": "https://x.com/mikehtrujillo/status/2123910888071799131",
            "lang": "en",
            "createdAt": "2026-11-20T22:46:30.000Z",
            "conversationId": "2123910888071799131",
            "inReplyToId": null,
            "author": {
              "id": "624826831",
              "username": "mikehtrujillo",
              "name": "Michael Trujillo",
              "verified": true,
              "followersCount": 7987,
              "profileImageUrl": "https://pbs.twimg.com/profile_images/1291610404167147521/EJztaPDg_normal.jpg"
            },
            "likeCount": 4,
            "retweetCount": 0,
            "replyCount": 0,
            "viewCount": 2710,
            "quoteCount": 0,
            "bookmarkCount": 3,
            "media": [],
            "entities": {
              "hashtags": [],
              "mentions": [],
              "urls": []
            },
            "article": null
          },
          "retweetedPost": null
        },
        {
          "id": "2123966041311363429",
          "text": "Smaller districts means more competitive elections which forces all politicians to look beyond simply catering to low hanging fruit like HOAs and appeal to a broader swath of their districts. Sure, if we go to a council w/ 35+ reps districts could become polarized/localized.",
          "url": "https://x.com/UnrigLA/status/2123966041311363429",
          "lang": "en",
          "createdAt": "2026-11-21T02:25:40.000Z",
          "conversationId": "2123963723627077959",
          "inReplyToId": "2123964959050944820",
          "author": {
            "id": "1022564507971801088",
            "username": "UnrigLA",
            "name": "Unrig LA",
            "verified": false,
            "followersCount": 16613,
            "profileImageUrl": "https://pbs.twimg.com/profile_images/1179148691996721152/z38zFDv5_normal.jpg"
          },
          "likeCount": 3,
          "retweetCount": 0,
          "replyCount": 1,
          "viewCount": 191,
          "quoteCount": 0,
          "bookmarkCount": 0,
          "media": [],
          "entities": {
            "hashtags": [],
            "mentions": [],
            "urls": []
          },
          "article": null,
          "quotedPost": null,
          "retweetedPost": null
        },
        {
          "id": "2123966800757240298",
          "text": "No one on council is entertaining anything above 30 and we can always look at options that hedge against local fiefdoms like 1. A combo of districts and regions. Or 2. Proportional RCV w/ multi member districts (ex. 3 reps each CD like Portland).",
          "url": "https://x.com/UnrigLA/status/2123966800757240298",
          "lang": "en",
          "createdAt": "2026-11-21T02:28:41.000Z",
          "conversationId": "2123963723627077959",
          "inReplyToId": "2123966041311363429",
          "author": {
            "id": "1022564507971801088",
            "username": "UnrigLA",
            "name": "Unrig LA",
            "verified": false,
            "followersCount": 16613,
            "profileImageUrl": "https://pbs.twimg.com/profile_images/1179148691996721152/z38zFDv5_normal.jpg"
